msgid "When set, the rule uses lease mode: it claims chunks of up to this many permits from the store and serves requests from the chunk, trading admission precision for fewer store calls. The actual chunk adapts to the demand of this replica, and a chunk may be served for `lease-size` emission intervals (`window / permits`). At least 1, and no more than a static limit's burst; for resolved limits each chunk is capped to the selected burst. At most `permits / 20` is recommended, because every replica may strand up to one chunk. Requires a store other than `local`. When absent, every request makes one store call."
